  "Name": "Kumar2015-TiO2-Al2O3-610",
  "Source": "M. Kumar, N. Kumari, P. K. Rao, V. Karar, S. V. Ramagopal, and A. L. Sharma, \"Multi-layer dielectric thin-film optical filters for beam folding applications,\" Proc. SPIE 9654, 96540F (2015). doi:10.1117/12.2181776 - Sec. 2.1 text below Fig. 2 (p. 3): TiO2 75 nm, Al2O3 100 nm; substrate BK7 from Sec. 2.2; indices Table 1",
  "Notes": "Five-layer TiO2/Al2O3 folding mirror with peak reflectance ~64 % at 610 nm at 45 deg\nSpecification: Peak reflectance ~64 % at 610 nm at 45 deg incidence.\nReported: Text p. 3: simulated peak reflectance around 64 % at 610 nm (45 deg); measured peak 'close to 64 %' (p. 4). Fig. 2 simulated (approximate): R ~18 % at 400 nm, local maximum ~22 % near 415 nm, minimum ~9 % near 465 nm, ~45 % at 520 nm, broad maximum ~65-66 % around 600-610 nm, ~54 % at 700 nm. Fig. 4 measured: ~12 % at 400 nm, ~25 % at 430 nm, minimum ~15 % near 470 nm, ~63-64 % over 580-610 nm, ~47 % at 700 nm.\nNotes: HLHLH order (TiO2 outermost) assumed; the paper says only '5 layered TiO2-Al2O3'. TiO2 n = 2.3 (midpoint of the 2.2-2.4 range at 550 nm), Al2O3 n = 1.63, both non-dispersive. Unpolarised, 45 deg in air; the incoherent BK7 back side is presumably included as for Fig. 1. Total physical thickness 3x75 + 2x100 = 425 nm (not printed).\nLayers from Sec. 2.1 text below Fig. 2 (p. 3): TiO2 75 nm, Al2O3 100 nm; substrate BK7 from Sec. 2.2; indices Table 1; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours R peak 72.2 % at 627 nm, 45 deg, with the back surface; paper peak near 610 nm, R ~64 %. Peak 72 % against ~64 %: the paper gives TiO2 only as a range (2.2-2.4; 2.3 used here) and does not print the layer order, which is assumed HLHLH.",
